Subject: [PATCH] GPU renderer: vertex and mesh buffers grown without zeroing,
 triangles written in place

The frame's vertex list and mesh words were value-initialized on every resize (zeroed, then
written over at once), and triangles went in by push_back one vertex at a time. A
default-initializing allocator for those buffers and in-place writes into the room made for
them: about 4-5% more frames a second uncapped in Transformers (the GS thread the limit).
---
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp | 63 +++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp
index 478fdbc..faa0f9c 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/gs/gs_gpu.cpp
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
